{"Success":true,"Data":[{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.72.41.59","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78914,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"057d7dd1a2a5a6d5d7dd34f1db59682e","RawContent":"Ohhhh my experience was good but not always! Growing up AC was the only one who flew to our small northern town. Only within the last year or two WJ came in. That said I&#039;ve had issues with all airlines whether it be delays, lost baggage, over bookings, etc.  Thankfully the wedding went fairly smooth.  \n\n\nCosta Rica sounds wonderful. Everyone I know who has been lists it as their favorite.  \n\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1892104,"PostDate":1428360670,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                Ohhhh my experience was good but not always! Growing up AC was the only one who flew to our small northern town. Only within the last year or two WJ came in. That said I've had issues with all airlines whether it be delays, lost baggage, over bookings, etc.  Thankfully the wedding went fairly smooth.  <br><br>\nCosta Rica sounds wonderful. Everyone I know who has been lists it as their favorite.  <br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>Married on 2015\/01\/21 at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya with 43 guests in attendance \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Review\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399414202,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.48.47.201","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78914,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":1428415212,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"35676e182bd7729682ca63ee8716a3bf","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"kcole123\"]&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"acw271011\"]&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;@[member=\"calgarybride2015\"]&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;So glad your Travel went so smoothly with your wedding Kim! It is a huge stresser!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;So I have&amp;nbsp;calmed&amp;nbsp;down today....I called my TA this morning but she is off today..boo. So I went through emails that she sent me before when everyone booked...and the info in the ones she sent me and the ones AC sent back when they confirmed are correct...so it was&amp;nbsp;definitely&amp;nbsp;a mistake on AC end, but I still think the purpose of having a travel agent is to have her look at this stuff and make sure its correct before she sends it to me for my check, I spent all morning going through each persons&amp;nbsp;itinerary to find all the mistakes. I feel bad that I&#039;m shitting on my TA and I really shouldn&#039;t be this is the first thing she has let me down on so far, and I&#039;m sure once I talk to her tomorrow she will clear it all up for me.&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1892178,"PostDate":1428414634,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"277264\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/277264-kcole123\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">kcole123<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"232000\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/232000-acw271011\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">acw271011<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n<p>@<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"277873\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/277873-calgarybride2015\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">calgarybride2015<\/span><\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>So glad your Travel went so smoothly with your wedding Kim! It is a huge stresser!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>So I have\u00a0calmed\u00a0down today....I called my TA this morning but she is off today..boo. So I went through emails that she sent me before when everyone booked...and the info in the ones she sent me and the ones AC sent back when they confirmed are correct...so it was\u00a0definitely\u00a0a mistake on AC end, but I still think the purpose of having a travel agent is to have her look at this stuff and make sure its correct before she sends it to me for my check, I spent all morning going through each persons\u00a0itinerary to find all the mistakes. I feel bad that I'm shitting on my TA and I really shouldn't be this is the first thing she has let me down on so far, and I'm sure once I talk to her tomorrow she will clear it all up for me.\u00a0<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10765;116\/st\/20151125\/e\/Our+Wedding\/k\/461e\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78914-meandhim-grand-palladium-bavaro-nov-2015\/'>My Planning Thread<\/a>\u00a0- MeandHim - Grand Palladium Bavaro - Nov 25 2015","Email":"markandshavonne@live.com","IpAddress":"70.30.85.211","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1365777659,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-268499.jpg?_r=1395417550","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Meandhim","Id":268499,"Name":"Meandhim","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.48.47.201","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78914,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"970ad75fb8ec3787bf467dc6af18f5b3","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"&gt;Procrastination at its finest...that about sums me up!&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/span&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Legal Wedding \u2013 102 days&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Leaving for Punta Cana \u2013 221 Days&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Wedding Day \u2013 226 Days&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Legal Wedding \u2013 Update&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Speaking of Procrastination...we finally booked our tickets Home for July! I forgot to mention that the reason we are going home in July is actually because it is \u201cCome Home Year\u201d for the place where I grew up. The place I grew up is really, really, tiny (like 150 people tiny), so every 15 years or so, along with the 3 other communities close by, they organize a come home year. Come home Year is like a reunion of sorts....They plan a week of events...fishing derby\u2019s, concerts, cookouts, etc...and people who have moved away all plan to come home during that week...it\u2019s really fun. &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;So we get into St. John\u2019s Friday Night 1 am&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;We have to get Legally Married Sometime Saturday (TBD)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Sunday morning&amp;nbsp; 6am Leave to drive to My Home Town for a week (12hr Drive with my Parents and Nan!)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Now I need to find a marriage commissioner who is available that day and I need to get the Marriage Licence. Apparently you need to apply for it in person there and you need to get it to the marriage commissioner 3 days before the wedding....umm...just a slight snag ...but we are going home in June for my FI\u2019s Sisters Memorial so we will have to pick it up then I guess.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Now for Some of the Fun Stuff..&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;My Invites \/ Wedding Website&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;So far our Invitations are the DIY I\u2019m most proud of. I searched around on Pinterest and I found what I wanted...I think it was linked to an etsy seller but out of my price range. I thought....ok...I can do this..so I downloaded the trial version of Adobe illustrator...watched a few video\u2019s...(thank you YouTube!) and I was off...I will mention I do use Photoshop a lot at work so I wasn\u2019t really learning from scratch. I used Vistaprint postcard template and waited for a coupon..I got 100 postcards and envelopes for just under $30!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I have a friend who is a graphic designer and she gave me some helpful tips&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;1.\t   Don\u2019t use too many different Fonts \u2013 3 max \u2013 make sure they complement each other&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;2.\t   Pair a Script Font with a simpler font&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;3.\t   Make sure the Important info is the easiest to read&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;4.\t   Don\u2019t go crazy with colors&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Here\u2019s the result:&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;[sharedmedia=gallery:images:80903]&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;For our wedding website I used Weddingwire...it\u2019s a great website, not only can you make a website but you can create guestlists, budgets, other events, seating charts, RSVP, track gifts, registries, etc. I used the &lt;a data-ipb=&#039;nomediaparse&#039; href=&#039;http:\/\/www.weddingwire.com\/wedding-ideas\/wedding\/12-totally-gorgeous-destination-and-beach-wedding-website-designs&#039;&gt;Flights of fancy&lt;\/a&gt; (9 of 14, I think) design Template which kind of matched my Invite style. I must say the website was fun to make but realistically not many people really looked at it...I ended up making a secret Facebook group as well just because I knew that it would get the info out faster.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I have a Bunch of other stationary started \/ planned:&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:symbol;\"&gt;\u00b7\t\t &lt;\/span&gt;Resort Pocket Map \/ with Spanish Phrases - Started&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:symbol;\"&gt;\u00b7\t\t &lt;\/span&gt;Do not disturb sign - Started&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:symbol;\"&gt;\u00b7\t\t &lt;\/span&gt;I Spy Game \/ Scavenger hunt - Started&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:symbol;\"&gt;\u00b7\t\t &lt;\/span&gt;Luggage tag - Started&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:symbol;\"&gt;\u00b7\t\t &lt;\/span&gt;Welcome Letter&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:symbol;\"&gt;\u00b7\t\t &lt;\/span&gt;Menu&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:symbol;\"&gt;\u00b7\t\t &lt;\/span&gt;Program&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:symbol;\"&gt;\u00b7\t\t &lt;\/span&gt;Timeline&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:symbol;\"&gt;\u00b7\t\t &lt;\/span&gt;Madlibs \/ Trivia&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:symbol;\"&gt;\u00b7\t\t &lt;\/span&gt;Wedding facebook&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=\"font-family:symbol;\"&gt;\u00b7\t\t &lt;\/span&gt;Postcards \u2013 Might used this as the guest book...maybe - Started&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;This list is a little ambitious so we will see how far I actually get...haha!&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Next.....&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Dress&lt;\/strong&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Wedding Dress Shopping was not what I thought it would be. None of my close friends or family live in the same province as me so the first time I went dress shopping I went to Beckers Bridal in Toronto alone. The sales lady was nice...a little pushy for my liking...I felt like she was trying to convince me to buy a dress I liked but was not really in love with...which is her job I guess, but still not fun. The second time I went I went to David\u2019s Bridal with one of my Friends \/ Neighbours. It was a better experience as I had some to laugh at the things that looked ridiculous and someone to help me say no to the sales lady.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The dress I finally bought I found online at David\u2019s Bridal on Sale...I saw it online and loved it...unfortunately this dress was not available in Canada! Which meant I could not try it on, I could not have it shipped here and could not return it if it didn\u2019t fit. I called a few stores in NY that were within a reasonable driving distance but no one seemed to have that dress...I finally found a store that had one left&amp;nbsp; in size 12 (my street size at the time). It was too far to drive to the store but since the dress was only 199 USD I ordered it over the phone had it shipped to my FI\u2019s Sister in California who then sent it to me. It Fit! Well sort of...it\u2019s actually a little big for me...it fall straight down from the boobs. Alterations to be done:&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Darts to hug it closer to body in the front&lt;\/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Possible lining replacement, the current lining is a little see-thru.&lt;\/li&gt;\n&lt;\/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;Since my first dress was so inexpensive I decided that I wanted a second, shorter dress for the reception so I could dance a fast Irish waltz with my dad and not have to wear high heels. I bought this one at David\u2019s Bridal for $79 and I want a sparkly belt &amp;nbsp;to replace the ribbon.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I do have Dress Regret! Both My Dresses are in storage at my Soon-to-be brother-in-law\u2019s and I haven\u2019t tried them on since I bought them. I will have them both for almost 2 years when the wedding actually rolls around because of the date change and now I\u2019m wondering if could have done better. I\u2019m also losing weight...and I\u2019m afraid that the dress will be way too big. I don\u2019t have the room in the budget for another dress.&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;[sharedmedia=core:attachments:28577]&lt;\/div&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;More to come soon...with more Pictures...&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1892950,"PostDate":1428941199,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p><span  style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Procrastination at its finest...that about sums me up!\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Legal Wedding \u2013 102 days<\/p>\n<p>Leaving for Punta Cana \u2013 221 Days<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Day \u2013 226 Days<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong>The Legal Wedding \u2013 Update<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Speaking of Procrastination...we finally booked our tickets Home for July! I forgot to mention that the reason we are going home in July is actually because it is \u201cCome Home Year\u201d for the place where I grew up. The place I grew up is really, really, tiny (like 150 people tiny), so every 15 years or so, along with the 3 other communities close by, they organize a come home year. Come home Year is like a reunion of sorts....They plan a week of events...fishing derby\u2019s, concerts, cookouts, etc...and people who have moved away all plan to come home during that week...it\u2019s really fun. \u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>So we get into St. John\u2019s Friday Night 1 am<\/p>\n<p>We have to get Legally Married Sometime Saturday (TBD)<\/p>\n<p>Sunday morning\u00a0 6am Leave to drive to My Home Town for a week (12hr Drive with my Parents and Nan!)<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Now I need to find a marriage commissioner who is available that day and I need to get the Marriage Licence. Apparently you need to apply for it in person there and you need to get it to the marriage commissioner 3 days before the wedding....umm...just a slight snag ...but we are going home in June for my FI\u2019s Sisters Memorial so we will have to pick it up then I guess.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Now for Some of the Fun Stuff..<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong>My Invites \/ Wedding Website<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>So far our Invitations are the DIY I\u2019m most proud of. I searched around on Pinterest and I found what I wanted...I think it was linked to an etsy seller but out of my price range. I thought....ok...I can do this..so I downloaded the trial version of Adobe illustrator...watched a few video\u2019s...(thank you YouTube!) and I was off...I will mention I do use Photoshop a lot at work so I wasn\u2019t really learning from scratch. I used Vistaprint postcard template and waited for a coupon..I got 100 postcards and envelopes for just under $30!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I have a friend who is a graphic designer and she gave me some helpful tips<\/p>\n<p>1.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Don\u2019t use too many different Fonts \u2013 3 max \u2013 make sure they complement each other<\/p>\n<p>2.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Pair a Script Font with a simpler font<\/p>\n<p>3.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Make sure the Important info is the easiest to read<\/p>\n<p>4.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 Don\u2019t go crazy with colors<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Here\u2019s the result:<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><!-- bbcodeImage-js (do not remove or edit this tag) -->\n<a href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/gallery\/image\/80903-invite\/' class='bbc_url' title=''><img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/gallery\/album_17971\/sml_gallery_268499_17971_273919.jpg' class='galattach galimageview sharedmedia_screenshot' title='Invite'  width='127' height='200'  alt='Invite' id='sml_image_view_80903' \/><\/a>\n<br \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>For our wedding website I used Weddingwire...it\u2019s a great website, not only can you make a website but you can create guestlists, budgets, other events, seating charts, RSVP, track gifts, registries, etc. I used the <a href='http:\/\/www.weddingwire.com\/wedding-ideas\/wedding\/12-totally-gorgeous-destination-and-beach-wedding-website-designs' class='bbc_url' title='External link' rel='nofollow external'>Flights of fancy<\/a> (9 of 14, I think) design Template which kind of matched my Invite style. I must say the website was fun to make but realistically not many people really looked at it...I ended up making a secret Facebook group as well just because I knew that it would get the info out faster.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I have a Bunch of other stationary started \/ planned:<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:symbol\">\u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 <\/span>Resort Pocket Map \/ with Spanish Phrases - Started<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:symbol\">\u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 <\/span>Do not disturb sign - Started<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:symbol\">\u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 <\/span>I Spy Game \/ Scavenger hunt - Started<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:symbol\">\u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 <\/span>Luggage tag - Started<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:symbol\">\u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 <\/span>Welcome Letter<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:symbol\">\u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 <\/span>Menu<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:symbol\">\u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 <\/span>Program<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:symbol\">\u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 <\/span>Timeline<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:symbol\">\u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 <\/span>Madlibs \/ Trivia<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:symbol\">\u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 <\/span>Wedding facebook<\/p>\n<p><span  style=\"font-family:symbol\">\u00b7\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 <\/span>Postcards \u2013 Might used this as the guest book...maybe - Started<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>This list is a little ambitious so we will see how far I actually get...haha!\u00a0<\/p><br \/><p>Next.....<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><strong>The Dress<\/strong><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Dress Shopping was not what I thought it would be. None of my close friends or family live in the same province as me so the first time I went dress shopping I went to Beckers Bridal in Toronto alone. The sales lady was nice...a little pushy for my liking...I felt like she was trying to convince me to buy a dress I liked but was not really in love with...which is her job I guess, but still not fun. The second time I went I went to David\u2019s Bridal with one of my Friends \/ Neighbours. It was a better experience as I had some to laugh at the things that looked ridiculous and someone to help me say no to the sales lady.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>The dress I finally bought I found online at David\u2019s Bridal on Sale...I saw it online and loved it...unfortunately this dress was not available in Canada! Which meant I could not try it on, I could not have it shipped here and could not return it if it didn\u2019t fit. I called a few stores in NY that were within a reasonable driving distance but no one seemed to have that dress...I finally found a store that had one left\u00a0 in size 12 (my street size at the time). It was too far to drive to the store but since the dress was only 199 USD I ordered it over the phone had it shipped to my FI\u2019s Sister in California who then sent it to me. It Fit! Well sort of...it\u2019s actually a little big for me...it fall straight down from the boobs. Alterations to be done:<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<ul><li>Darts to hug it closer to body in the front<\/li>\n<li>Possible lining replacement, the current lining is a little see-thru.<\/li>\n<\/ul><p>Since my first dress was so inexpensive I decided that I wanted a second, shorter dress for the reception so I could dance a fast Irish waltz with my dad and not have to wear high heels. I bought this one at David\u2019s Bridal for $79 and I want a sparkly belt \u00a0to replace the ribbon.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I do have Dress Regret! Both My Dresses are in storage at my Soon-to-be brother-in-law\u2019s and I haven\u2019t tried them on since I bought them. I will have them both for almost 2 years when the wedding actually rolls around because of the date change and now I\u2019m wondering if could have done better. I\u2019m also losing weight...and I\u2019m afraid that the dress will be way too big. I don\u2019t have the room in the budget for another dress.<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<div><a class='resized_img' rel='lightbox[1860168]' id='ipb-attach-url-28577-0-47747400-1429015425' href=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_07_2014\/post-268499-0-07659800-1405531792.jpg\" title=\"Dress 8.jpg - Size: 154.38KB\"><span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' itemprop=\"image\" src=\"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/monthly_07_2014\/post-268499-0-07659800-1405531792_thumb.jpg\" id='ipb-attach-img-28577-0-47747400-1429015425' style='width:150;height:133' class='attach' width=\"150\" height=\"133\" alt=\"Dress 8.jpg\" \/><\/span><\/a>\n<\/div><br \/><p>More to come soon...with more Pictures...<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10765;116\/st\/20151125\/e\/Our+Wedding\/k\/461e\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78914-meandhim-grand-palladium-bavaro-nov-2015\/'>My Planning Thread<\/a>\u00a0- MeandHim - Grand Palladium Bavaro - Nov 25 2015","Email":"markandshavonne@live.com","IpAddress":"70.30.85.211","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1365777659,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-268499.jpg?_r=1395417550","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Meandhim","Id":268499,"Name":"Meandhim","IsOnline":true}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"70.72.41.59","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78914,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"3dc6171df768953440098327879f3b06","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt;Great update!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I personally love both of your dresses!!! &amp;nbsp;Sometimes it&#039;s hard not to think of others or want to look for others, I would recommend reminding yourself why you chose those in the first place to help you thru those times of regret. I would also suggest you put the dress on but I know with where it&#039;s stored that isn&#039;t the easiest for you!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I LOVE your STDS!!! &amp;nbsp;Great job! &amp;nbsp;I wish I was crafty enough for something like that :)&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I had a postcard guestbook and thought it was a fantastic idea, but of course I am bias! &amp;nbsp;I actually came up with the idea before I ever found BDW, so I was a bit upset to realize it wasn&#039;t a Kim original idea heheh!!!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;I remember back last summer when I said &#039;man I have to wait 7 months!!!!&#039; now I have been married almost 3 months - all I can say is that time flies!!!&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Congrats on knowing when your legal is going to be!!!! &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1892971,"PostDate":1428958251,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p>Great update!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I personally love both of your dresses!!! \u00a0Sometimes it's hard not to think of others or want to look for others, I would recommend reminding yourself why you chose those in the first place to help you thru those times of regret. I would also suggest you put the dress on but I know with where it's stored that isn't the easiest for you!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I LOVE your STDS!!! \u00a0Great job! \u00a0I wish I was crafty enough for something like that <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I had a postcard guestbook and thought it was a fantastic idea, but of course I am bias! \u00a0I actually came up with the idea before I ever found BDW, so I was a bit upset to realize it wasn't a Kim original idea heheh!!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>I remember back last summer when I said 'man I have to wait 7 months!!!!' now I have been married almost 3 months - all I can say is that time flies!!!<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Congrats on knowing when your legal is going to be!!!! \u00a0<\/p>\n\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>-Kim<\/p>\n<p>Married on 2015\/01\/21 at the Grand Sirenis Riviera Maya with 43 guests in attendance \u00a0 <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Planning Thread -\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Pictures\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78209-calgarybride2015s-planning-thread-15121-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya\/page-36<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>Wedding Review\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/38741-grand-sirenis-riviera-maya-brides\/page-131#entry1885600<\/a><\/p>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p>\u00a0","Email":"kdeakin@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"68.145.235.0","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1399414202,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-277873.jpg?_r=1422218225","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":134,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"calgarybride2015","Id":277873,"Name":"calgarybride2015","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"174.117.36.109","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":78914,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":1,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"de4e5f3ffd4ca541ca27bcb56e9b76a9","RawContent":"@[member=\"calgarybride2015\"] thanks! I draw all day at work so I don&#039;t consider that being crafty... You my friend ARE crazy crafty!  All your DIY&#039;s were amazing and inspiring...and I&#039;m sure you will see a few of your ideas copied here!! \n\n\nI haven&#039;t completely nailed down the guestbook yet but postcards are high on the list so far thanks to you. I&#039;m definitely making postcards but I might just put them in the welcome bags if I come up with another idea for my guest book.\n\n\nI&#039;ve had a ton of original ideas until I joined here and then realized someone else did it already.. Lol\n\n\nAs for the dresses I&#039;m trying not to watch say yes to the dress or any other wedding show \/ magazine... It just sets in the doubt. I&#039;m sure my dress is fine and once the time comes and everything is together it&#039;ll be great!\n\n\nI know the 7 months are going to fly by and as I mentioned above and you can probably tell by my few posts I&#039;m a total procrastinator! I&#039;m terrified I&#039;m going to have too much left til the end...current goal get legal stuff sorted SOON, before the end of April. \n\n\n\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk","Attachments":[],"Id":1892979,"PostDate":1428959471,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                @<a hovercard-ref=\"member\" hovercard-id=\"277873\" data-ipb=\"noparse\" class=\"_hovertrigger url fn name  bbc_member\" href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/user\/277873-calgarybride2015\/' title='Member profile'><span itemprop=\"name\">calgarybride2015<\/span><\/a> thanks! I draw all day at work so I don't consider that being crafty... You my friend ARE crazy crafty!  All your DIY's were amazing and inspiring...and I'm sure you will see a few of your ideas copied here!! <br><br>\nI haven't completely nailed down the guestbook yet but postcards are high on the list so far thanks to you. I'm definitely making postcards but I might just put them in the welcome bags if I come up with another idea for my guest book.<br><br>\nI've had a ton of original ideas until I joined here and then realized someone else did it already.. Lol<br><br>\nAs for the dresses I'm trying not to watch say yes to the dress or any other wedding show \/ magazine... It just sets in the doubt. I'm sure my dress is fine and once the time comes and everything is together it'll be great!<br><br>\nI know the 7 months are going to fly by and as I mentioned above and you can probably tell by my few posts I'm a total procrastinator! I'm terrified I'm going to have too much left til the end...current goal get legal stuff sorted SOON, before the end of April. <br><br><br>\nSent from my iPhone using Tapatalk\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<div><a  class=\"bbc_url\" href=\"http:\/\/www.TickerFactory.com\/\"><img src=\"http:\/\/tickers.TickerFactory.com\/ezt\/d\/4;10765;116\/st\/20151125\/e\/Our+Wedding\/k\/461e\/event.png\" alt=\"event.png\"><\/a><\/div>\n<div>\u00a0<\/div>\n<p>\u00a0<\/p>\n<p><a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/78914-meandhim-grand-palladium-bavaro-nov-2015\/'>My Planning Thread<\/a>\u00a0- MeandHim - Grand Palladium Bavaro - Nov 25 2015","Email":"markandshavonne@live.com","IpAddress":"70.30.85.211","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1365777659,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-268499.jpg?_r=1395417550","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":200,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Meandhim","Id":268499,"Name":"Meandhim","IsOnline":true}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":25,"TotalPages":3,"CurrentPage":20,"NextPage":-1,"PreviousPage":10,"LastPage":20},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":0,"Type":"int"}]}
